<title>USA: Woodland Hills, Pa., $58 mln school budget fails.</title>
<headline>Woodland Hills, Pa., $58 mln school budget fails.</headline>
<dateline>WOODLAND HILLS, Pa. 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the second time in a week, the Woodland Hills, Pa., school district failed to approve a new budget for the 1997-98 school year.</p>
<p>Another budget hearing is scheduled for next week on the $58 million spending proposal, according to local officials.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
